TYPES.md §7.4: a regex refinement is an RE2 search, through an alias too, checked on computed
strings: /[a-z]/ matches ABc anywhere, /^[1-9]:[1-9]$/ refuses 2x2.
-- teamboard/taxonomy.canon --
package teamboard

type Layout = String(/^[1-9]:[1-9]$/)

record Deck {
  layouts: [Layout]
  nick: String(/[a-z]/)
}

let deck: Deck = { layouts: ["4:1", "2" + "x2"], nick: "AB" + "c" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3205]  teamboard/taxonomy.canon:10:37
  deck.layouts[1]: 2x2 does not match /^[1-9]:[1-9]$/
  expected by teamboard/taxonomy.canon:3 (String(/^[1-9]:[1-9]$/))

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
